WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
A swarm can agree on a release and still lack the evidence or authority to perform it.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Authenticity. Applicability. Current authorization. A trustworthy system checks all three.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Fleet Witness traces the recommendation, the controller decision, and the actual database effect.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:42.000
This is the actual seed-42 viewer. Its deterministic agents illustrate the mechanism; they are not measured models.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Here the reviewer promotes a genuine build receipt into a release-safety claim. The raw supervisor approves.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:05.000
The recommendation is incorrect. The controller denies execution: a build receipt does not prove release safety.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Switch to the paired scope-explicit presentation. The scripted supervisor now denies this unsupported release.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:26.000
This recommendation was valid at its snapshot. Permission is revoked before the execution attempt.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:38.000
The controller checks current permission and blocks the revoked attempt. No release record is committed.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:50.000
An authorized duplicate request is a no-op. A release here is a local SQLite record, not a public deployment.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:02.000
A separate recorded study used one real supervisor with synthetic workers and reviewers: 160 trials in 80 pairs.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Raw: 18 invalid approvals. Scope explicit: zero invalid approvals, but 40 invalid denials—it denied every request.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:30.000
All invalid and revoked attempts were blocked. Thirty authorized effects committed. These are synthetic, local tasks.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:42.000
One offline command checks every packaged hash, compares repository sources, and recomputes the frozen trial totals.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:52.000
Run the offline demo and finite checker. The report also distinguishes the separate historical two-model study.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Limits remain: synthetic tasks, local effects, incomplete historical provenance, and no uncontrolled web observation.

